    "# Week 10 — Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
    "UCI Online Shoppers Purchasing Intention (dataset 468). Run from the repository root after downloading the data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import os, subprocess, sys\n",
    "REPO_DIR = Path('/content/online-shoppers-nn2026')\n",
    "if not (REPO_DIR / 'src').exists():\n",
    "    subprocess.run(['git', 'clone', '--branch', 'main', 'https://github.com/azzzzzzzzzzo57-star/online-shoppers-nn2026.git', str(REPO_DIR)], check=True)\n",
    "os.chdir(REPO_DIR)\n",
    "subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', '-q', 'ucimlrepo==0.0.7', 'pandas==2.2.3', 'matplotlib==3.10.0'], check=True)\n",
    "if not (REPO_DIR / 'data/raw/online_shoppers.csv').exists():\n",
    "    subprocess.run([sys.executable, 'data/download_data.py'], check=True)\n",
    "print('Repository ready:', REPO_DIR)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "ROOT = Path.cwd()\n",
    "if not (ROOT / 'data').exists(): ROOT = ROOT.parent\n",
    "DATA_PATH = ROOT / 'data' / 'raw' / 'online_shoppers.csv'\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n",
    "print('Dataset shape:', df.shape)\n",
    "display(df.head())\n",
    "print('\\nColumn data types:')\n",
    "display(df.dtypes.to_frame('dtype'))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Dataset structure and data quality\n",
    "Check row/column counts, missing values, exact duplicates, and descriptive statistics. Exact duplicates are removed by the preprocessing pipeline before splitting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('Missing values by column:')\n",
    "display(df.isna().sum().sort_values(ascending=False).to_frame('missing_count'))\n",
    "print('Total missing cells:', int(df.isna().sum().sum()))\n",
    "print('Exact duplicate rows:', int(df.duplicated().sum()))\n",
    "display(df.describe(include='all').T)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Target distribution and class imbalance\n",
    "`Revenue=True` is the minority purchase class. The primary metric is macro-F1; per-class recall is also important because accuracy alone can hide poor purchase detection."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "target_counts = df['Revenue'].value_counts(dropna=False).sort_index()\n",
    "target_summary = pd.DataFrame({'count': target_counts, 'percentage': (target_counts / len(df) * 100).round(2)})\n",
    "display(target_summary)\n",
    "ax = target_counts.rename(index={False:'No purchase', True:'Purchase'}).plot(kind='bar', rot=0, title='Revenue class distribution')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Sessions'); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
    "print('Minority-class share:', f\"{df['Revenue'].mean():.2%}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
